WHY AGPL
--------

pdn-qso links M0LTE.Flex (AGPL-3.0) for the FlexRadio device, so the combined
work is AGPL-3.0-or-later.  It also links pdn-soundmodem (GPL-3.0-or-later),
which GPLv3 section 13 expressly permits to be combined with AGPL-3.0 code.

BUNDLED THIRD-PARTY COMPONENTS
------------------------------

The executable statically bundles the .NET runtime and libraries
(Copyright (c) .NET Foundation and Contributors, MIT licence) together with
Terminal.Gui (MIT), pdn-soundmodem (GPL-3.0-or-later) and the Packet.NET support
packages it brings with it, and M0LTE.Flex (AGPL-3.0).  All are licence
compatible with AGPL-3.0-or-later.  Their individual licence texts are
distributed with their respective upstream sources.

PROVENANCE
----------

The LT fountain code in PdnQso.Link is implemented from Luby's 2002 paper and
MacKay's description of the robust soliton distribution, not ported from any
implementation.  RaptorQ is deliberately not used.
